<title>INDIA: India produced 3,645 T copper cathodes in April.</title>
<headline>India produced 3,645 T copper cathodes in April.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Hindustan Copper Ltd (HCL) produced 3,645 tonnes of copper cathodes in April 1997 compared with 3,275 in the same month in 1996, a government statement said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>HCL also produced 2,300 tonnes of continous cast copper rods in April 1997 against 2,445 tonnes in April 1996, the statement said.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	    Installed		  Production</p>
<p>	    capacity	   April 1997    April 1996</p>
<p>	    (annual)</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> cathodes   47,500	    3,645		3,275</p>
<p>Copper</p>
<p> rods	 60,000	    2,300		2,445</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes.</p>
